Maybe thanks to the… rotation of our planet?', 721.529, 727.240, NULL),
  (12268, 109, 'That’s right. Scientists think the origin
of dreaming just might have to do with the', 727.240, 731.330, NULL),
  (12269, 109, 'sheer amount of time that humans – and all
animals – spend in the dark.', 731.330, 736.720, NULL),
  (12270, 109, 'Our ability to use our peepers and see the
world around us is an extremely important', 736.720, 741.480, NULL),
  (12271, 109, 'evolutionary advantage. And because it’s
so important, the part of the brain responsible', 741.480, 746.350, NULL),
  (12272, 109, 'for sight, called the visual cortex, takes
up a big chunk of our brains.', 746.350, 751.100, NULL),
  (12273, 109, 'But there’s the thing. Our brains can also
be rewired pretty easily. If you were blindfolded,', 751.100, 757.470, NULL),
  (12274, 109, 'your brain would begin to change within an
hour of not using your sight. The neurons', 757.470, 762.329, NULL),
  (12275, 109, 'of the visual cortex start being taken over
for other tasks.', 762.329, 766.649, NULL),
  (12276, 109, 'The lengthy darkness of nighttime, would have
meant that the visual cortex of our human', 766.649, 770.769, NULL),
  (12277, 109, 'ancestors was at a high risk of being taken
over by other functions while we slept. If', 770.769, 776.600, NULL),
  (12278, 109, 'we didn’t use it, we could lose it. Dreams,
and their highly visual nature, may have evolved', 776.600, 782.470, NULL),
  (12279, 109, 'in mammals to keep these vulnerable brain
areas active at night… And keep the brain', 782.470, 787.330, NULL),
  (12280, 109, 'from rewiring itself in unfortunate ways.
So… which is it? Is it problem-solving,', 787.330, 793.769, NULL),
  (12281, 109, 'or practicing, or seeing, or is it problem
solving or not about seeing, or a bit about', 793.769, 801.959, NULL),
  (12282, 109, 'practicing and a pinch of problems solving?
Scientists don’t know if one or many of', 801.959, 808.950, NULL),
  (12283, 109, 'these ideas will prove to be correct, and
so research continues. Ah, science.  Always', 808.950, 815.161, NULL),
  (12284, 109, 'figuring stuff out. But never quite figuring
stuff out all the way.', 815.161, 819.420, NULL),
  (12285, 109, 'It’s even possible that dreams may have
evolved for one function, but stayed around', 819.420, 823.240, NULL),
  (12286, 109, 'so long because dreaming ended up helping
us in a bunch of other different ways.  Trying', 823.240, 827.579, NULL),
  (12287, 109, 'to peer into the workings of the sleeping
brain is one of the most challenging problems', 827.579, 832.779, NULL),
  (12288, 109, 'in psychology and neuroscience, but we’re
building a fuller and fuller picture of the', 832.779, 838.199, NULL),
  (12289, 109, 'science of dreaming, one dream …at a time.
You wouldn’t believe the dream I just had.', 838.199, 873.760, NULL),
